= Discourse (linguistics) — Simple =

In linguistics, '''discourse''' is language used in a larger connected situation, not just one isolated word or sentence.

A conversation is discourse. A story can be discourse. A debate, interview, article, or signed conversation can also be discourse.

People studying discourse ask how parts fit together, how speakers take turns, how topics change, how earlier information affects later language, and how the social situation matters.

[[Context (linguistics)/Simple|Context]] and [[Common ground/Simple|common ground]] are important because people interpret each new part using what has already happened.

This page is about language. The software platform called Discourse is a different subject: [[Discourse]].

